+# AutoVideo 7.0.94: image requests can pass Flow's credit approval guard; early waits are logged
+
+**Status: fixture-tested only.** The approval and wait behaviour is verified with fakes in
+`tests/test_v794_image_approval.py`. It has NOT been verified against live Flow. Watch the first image run
+after installing.
+
+**Default split size: 2400 characters** per Gemini TTS request (unchanged from 7.0.82).
+
+## Why
+
+Job `20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729`, shot_023 opening frame, 19:18-19:23 IST on 2026-10-25:
+
+- The 7.0.93 fresh-request loop made three submissions, each in a new project, and then stopped at the cap of 3.
+- Each wait logged "Waiting up to 360s", but two of them returned after about 43 s and the third after about 1 s.
+  Nothing was logged about why.
+- Cause in code: image requests set the approval journal but never the outstanding request id. The approval probe
+  refused every card at its first check ("no outstanding request; unsolicited approval refused"). The wait then
+  returned `False` with no log line.
+
+The 19:27 recovery run in a new process waited the full six minutes and still found no image in project
+`ca1709fe`. That is a separate open question. The new logs will show what Flow is doing.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Image approvals use the video credit guard.** An image request sets its own request id before submitting and
+  before recovery waits. A card is clicked only when it shows a visible cost at or below `max_generation_credits`
+  (0 for images), and only once per request. A card with no visible cost is never clicked. A paid card is refused
+  and logged as a credit-guard block.
+- **Reservations are kept.** Approval reservations written during a wait are copied back into the in-memory request
+  before any journal write, so a later write cannot drop them and allow a second click.
+- **Approval refusals and timeouts are logged.** A refused approval prints `[Flow] Approval refused: <reason>` and
+  the wait ends. A wait that runs out of time prints `[Flow] Wait ended after <n>s ...`. Some other early exits in the
+  same loop still return without a log line; they are not covered by this release.
+- Unchanged: the fresh-request cap (3 per shot), the rule that two real outputs stay blocked, the rule that video is
+  never resubmitted automatically, and the Resume gate.
+
+## Job 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729 (shot_023)
+
+These steps run on your machine, after installing 7.0.94. Nothing is run from this zip.
+
+1. Archive the saved request. It is kept on record, not deleted. Image requests cost no Flow credits, but this command
+   still asks for the credit flag. Run it only if you approve the one additional submission:
+
+       python3 cli.py v3 archive-request 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729 storyboard/shot_023_open.jpg --confirm-new-credit-spend
+
+2. Resume. With no journal left for shot_023, this makes one new image submission. If it produces no image, the
+   per-shot cap of 3 stops it again, with an explicit reason.
+
+       python3 cli.py v3 resume 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729
+
+## Update
+
+From the installation folder, after extracting this zip beside it. The installation must be 7.0.93 (run the 7.0.93
+update first if it is older):
+
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.94/tools/update_v793_to_v794.py .            # dry run
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.94/tools/update_v793_to_v794.py . --apply    # install
+
+Stop the dashboard first. Outputs, saved jobs and browser profiles are not touched.
